Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:46:40 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: Add Tensor G4 USI compatible

Google's zumapro-usi.dtsi describes the USIv2 mode selector used by
Tensor G4. The existing Exynos850 fallback selects the same two-clock,
three-mode USIv2 register interface already used by gs101 and gs201;
no new driver data or register layout is needed.

Retain the existing fallback layouts. This identity does not enable a
bus, change a protocol selector or initialize hardware. The PERIC0
clock provider and board resources remain separate dependencies.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/zumapro/+/8831630eee2ad095b85ed452944e6353940966a5/dts/zumapro-usi.dtsi

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-usi.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-usi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-usi.yaml
index 3e0941f99..9a2a8867b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-usi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-usi.yaml
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ properties:
           - enum:
               - google,gs101-usi
               - google,gs201-usi
+              - google,zumapro-usi
               - samsung,exynos2200-usi
               - samsung,exynosautov9-usi
               - samsung,exynosautov920-usi
